    <p><strong>John Barry's</strong> four wins span a remarkable 24-year career arc (1966&ndash;1990), the longest active winning span among the leaders. His gap of 17 years between his second win (<em>The Lion in Winter</em>, 1968) and third (<em>Out of Africa</em>, 1985) is one of the most dramatic comebacks in the category's history.</p>
    <p><strong>John Williams</strong> achieved his four wins in an 18-year window (1975&ndash;1993), including back-to-back wins for <em>Jaws</em> and <em>Star Wars</em>, two films that redefined the modern blockbuster score.</p>
    <p><strong>Ludwig G&ouml;ransson</strong> is the most recent entrant to the four-win tier, accumulating his wins in just eight years (2018&ndash;2026)&mdash;the fastest ascent to four wins in Oscar history. See the data note above regarding the 2023/2024 entries.</p>

